---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
List recent runs (the default when `snouty runs` runs with no subcommand).

Columns: RUN ID, STATUS, CREATED, LAUNCHER, RUN. RUN is the test name. For a run
with no test name, RUN is the first line of its description, or `-` when it has
none. `detail` prints the full description.

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each run prints as one JSON object on
its own line, in the order the server returns them:
  snouty --json runs list | jq -r .run_id

Usage: snouty runs list [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -s, --status <STATUS>
          Filter by status (starting, in_progress, completed, cancelled,
          incomplete, unknown)

  -l, --launcher <LAUNCHER>
          Filter by launcher name

      --created-after <CREATED_AFTER>
          Only show runs created after this timestamp (ISO 8601)

      --created-before <CREATED_BEFORE>
          Only show runs created before this timestamp (ISO 8601)

  -n, --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of runs to display
          
          [default: 10]

  -d, --detail
          Show a detailed key-value block per run, including the full
          description

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
